{
  "tema": 5914,
  "slug": "condicional-tener-que",
  "titulo": "Conjugate tener que (would have to) in the conditional",
  "subtitulo": "Tendría que firmar: what you would have to do.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Tener que in the conditional uses the stem tendr-: tendría, tendrías, tendría, tendríamos, tendrían + que + infinitive.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Tener que** + infinitive means _to have to_. In the conditional it means _would have to_. **Tener** is irregular here: add the conditional endings to the stem **tendr-**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**tendr-** + **-ía**…",
            "**que**",
            "infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "tener que"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "tendría que"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "tendrías que"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "tendría que"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "tendríamos que"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "tendrían que"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **que** can never be left out."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **tendría que** is a chain of three links: tendría, **que**, infinitive. Lose one and the chain breaks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Yo ==tendría que firmar== ese contrato millonario.",
              "en": "I'd have to sign that million-dollar contract."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tú ==tendrías que tomarte== una selfie en el arco de Tijuana.",
              "en": "You'd have to take a selfie at the Tijuana arch."
            },
            {
              "es": "El alumno ==tendría que repasar== para subir sus calificaciones.",
              "en": "The student would have to review to raise his grades."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nosotros ==tendríamos que ganar== más dinero.",
              "en": "We'd have to earn more money."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ellos ==tendrían que trabajar== los fines de semana.",
              "en": "They'd have to work on weekends."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ==tendrían que pagar== un diez por ciento de depósito.",
              "en": "You'd have to pay a ten percent deposit."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
